.TH NCURSYS 1 "October 2026" "ncursys 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ncursys \- terminal tool for visualizing hard disk usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ncursys
.I path
.RB [ --threads=N ]
.RB [ -x ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ncursys is an interactive terminal application for visualizing disk
usage as a navigable tree, built with glib and ncurses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I path
Required. The directory path to scan.
.TP
.BI --threads= N
Optional. Number of worker threads to use (default: number of CPUs + 2).
.TP
.BR -x ", " --one-file-system
Optional. Skip directories on different file systems, like
.BR "du -x" .
.SH NOTES
Sizes are computed like
.BR du (1):
allocated blocks are counted, directories included, and a file with
several hard links is counted only once.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by Dimitris Trivizakis.
